{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL1Ksn51oHCC1hEakkM", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told.\n\n- **Nightly run:** `review.run` crashed at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)`, which is before it records findings or sends any alerts. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\" and has no alert step. No findings file was written either, so nothing about it is stored anywhere.\n- **My session:** I didn't run the pipeline. The only thing I ran was the unit tests, which use their own temporary spool and fake `@example.com` recipients. There's no `spool/` directory in the repo.\n\nSo the finance on-call hasn't heard that the `expand` step spent $412.30 against its $250 budget. I can't see the runner's spool or the relay, and I can't rule out someone hearing about it some other way, but nothing in this repo or its log suggests they did.\n\nThat matters because the alert is late, not just held back. The README's policy assumes the on-call gets told about overspends, and the crash quietly stopped that. Because of your no-messages rule I haven't contacted anyone. I'd suggest that you, or whoever owns the job, tell the finance on-call about this finding directly, whatever we decide about the rerun."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d1cf74f7-c5c6-4492-ac84-9fd7d7efe3ce", "uuid": "a427f593-3efa-4dea-b70c-948eff3f3de1", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:22.046Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL1KcefhdpcJusGmeMK"}
